  "archive_readme": "https://github.com/andreiramani/pgvector_pgsql_windows\r\n------------------------------------------------------\r\n\r\n- ONLY for PostgreSQL v17 - Windows x64\r\n- Stop PostgreSQL using services.msc\r\n- Extract the zip file to your Postgres installed folder\r\n- Start PostgreSQL service\r\n- Run query: \r\nCREATE EXTENSION vector\r\n- Run this query to check if the extension is enable (t):\r\nSELECT extname,extrelocatable,extversion FROM pg_extension where extname='vector'\r\n\r\n\r\n=============================\r\nUPGRADE FROM PREVIOUS VERSION\r\n=============================\r\n- Stop PostgreSQL using services.msc\r\n- Extract the zip file to your Postgres installed folder, on overwrite dialog option, choose \"Yes to all\"\r\n- Start PostgreSQL service\r\n- Run query: \r\nALTER EXTENSION vector UPDATE\r\n- Check the version in the current database with:\r\nSELECT extversion FROM pg_extension WHERE extname = 'vector'\r\n\r\n",
  "readme_review": "Targets PostgreSQL 17 Windows x64. Broad extraction, overwrite and service restart instructions are deliberately not used; only allowlisted extension files are copied to the dedicated project runtime without overwriting different content.",
